        "summary": "In CH3CN at room temperature, 2 shows typical NIR Nd3+ emission (899, 1063, 1340 nm) via ligand-centered excitation; τ = 5.10 μs, Φem = 0.77%, ΦLn = 2.0%. It exhibits NIR luminescent sensing of anions, especially CN− and OAc− at ppm level (KSV 2.53×10^4 and 1.76×10^4 M−1; LOD 2.31 and 3.27 μM). Emission at 1063 nm drops >50% at 30.65 μM CN− or 51.12 μM OAc−; Φem falls to 0.32% after 30.65 μM CN−. UV–vis titration shows a new ~405 nm absorption with CN−.",
